1
00:00:05,220 --> 00:00:06,280
Hello again!

2
00:00:06,640 --> 00:00:08,197
You're listening to Mariah Radio,

3
00:00:08,280 --> 00:00:11,917
and we've got another rousing
segment for your aural pleasure.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:13,900
Help, Midnight Mentor!

5
00:00:14,220 --> 00:00:19,277
Our first letter is coming to
you from Forever 21, Pretty Baby.

6
00:00:19,360 --> 00:00:20,860
Kai, get a load of this.

7
00:00:21,140 --> 00:00:24,737
Once again, I was late to my little
rendezvous because of that thing.

8
00:00:24,820 --> 00:00:25,820
You know the one.

9
00:00:26,720 --> 00:00:27,550
Exactly!

10
00:00:27,633 --> 00:00:28,960
The one by the station!

11
00:00:29,300 --> 00:00:32,241
The crossing that never
opens when you need it to!

12
00:00:32,440 --> 00:00:33,675
It's just gonna be...

13
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:38,330
Whoa!

14
00:00:38,413 --> 00:00:40,792
Tell me how you really feel, pretty baby!

15
00:00:42,920 --> 00:00:43,750
Uh...

16
00:02:00,060 --> 00:02:01,080
You serious?

17
00:02:03,240 --> 00:02:07,475
So I guess we aren't the only stand
users at this school after all, huh?

18
00:02:08,280 --> 00:02:09,110
Right.

19
00:02:09,193 --> 00:02:11,820
Toshikazu Hazamada enrolled
as a junior in Group C.

20
00:02:12,360 --> 00:02:13,190
Apparently,

21
00:02:13,273 --> 00:02:15,437
he and his buddy had a
falling out over something

22
00:02:15,520 --> 00:02:18,260
trivial right before
the spring term started.

23
00:02:18,520 --> 00:02:22,677
Seems the friend dissed Hazemada's
favorite idol or anime or something.

24
00:02:22,760 --> 00:02:24,917
Normally, that'd be nothing
to write home about,

25
00:02:25,000 --> 00:02:27,917
but everything changed one
night when the friend he was

26
00:02:28,000 --> 00:02:31,588
arguing with gouged out his own
eye with a mechanical pencil.

27
00:02:32,600 --> 00:02:33,980
It's crazy, right?

28
00:02:34,660 --> 00:02:38,040
I hear Hazemada's friend
said this in the hospital.

29
00:02:38,700 --> 00:02:44,700
When I came to, I was staring at my eyeball
in my hand with the only eye I had left.

30
00:02:46,580 --> 00:02:49,177
So you're saying this guy
ripped out his friend's

31
00:02:49,260 --> 00:02:52,142
eye and he used some kind
of stand to do the job?

32
00:02:52,400 --> 00:02:57,017
Well, that could be what happened here,
but there's no surefire way to find out.

33
00:02:57,100 --> 00:03:00,237
Remember, the average person
isn't able to see a stand.

34
00:03:00,320 --> 00:03:01,438
Yeah, I don't know.

35
00:03:01,620 --> 00:03:03,267
This all sounds fishy to me.

36
00:03:03,440 --> 00:03:04,734
What did you just say?

37
00:03:05,060 --> 00:03:05,890
Chosuke,

38
00:03:05,973 --> 00:03:08,957
I don't know who you think you are, but
you've got no right to say that to me.

39
00:03:09,040 --> 00:03:11,017
I've got a real job now, you know.

40
00:03:11,100 --> 00:03:13,137
Hang on, you're actually working now?

41
00:03:13,220 --> 00:03:14,260
Of course I am.

42
00:03:14,460 --> 00:03:18,820
I managed to land myself a sweet
little gig in finance. Finance, huh?

43
00:03:19,320 --> 00:03:22,317
You sure that isn't code
for Lone Shark or something?

44
00:03:22,400 --> 00:03:25,812
For now, let's just say I'm
working with some good people.

45
00:03:26,680 --> 00:03:28,717
That's great, but did
you forget about this?

46
00:03:28,800 --> 00:03:30,035
We've got work to do.

47
00:03:32,360 --> 00:03:33,460
Wait up, Josuke!

48
00:03:34,220 --> 00:03:35,180
Master Koichi!

49
00:03:35,540 --> 00:03:37,305
You're seriously gonna go too?

50
00:03:37,640 --> 00:03:40,120
Just let that jackass Josuke handle it!

51
00:03:40,620 --> 00:03:41,980
I have to do this.

52
00:03:42,220 --> 00:03:44,455
Something evil's taking over our town.

53
00:03:44,540 --> 00:03:46,220
And if Morioh's in danger,

54
00:03:46,480 --> 00:03:47,540
then my mom,

55
00:03:47,780 --> 00:03:52,192
dad, sis, and pretty much everyone else
I care about are in danger as well.

56
00:03:52,280 --> 00:03:54,480
I'm scared, but it has to be done.

57
00:03:57,360 --> 00:03:58,190
Wow.

58
00:03:58,273 --> 00:03:59,420
What a gutsy thing to say.

59
00:03:59,860 --> 00:04:02,978
Then again, I would expect
nothing less from my hero.

60
00:04:03,780 --> 00:04:04,640
But still.

61
00:04:05,740 --> 00:04:08,777
You guys will have to excuse
me as I've got to get home now.

62
00:04:08,860 --> 00:04:10,919
Stay out of trouble, Master Koichi!

63
00:04:20,900 --> 00:04:23,377
It doesn't look like he's
hiding out in this room.

64
00:04:23,460 --> 00:04:26,197
Honestly, it'd be kind of
creepy if he was in here.

65
00:04:26,280 --> 00:04:29,117
Him coming back to school and
acting like nothing happened.

66
00:04:29,200 --> 00:04:32,729
Especially after digging out
his friend's eye with a pencil.

67
00:04:33,900 --> 00:04:36,720
Guys like that are psychos.

68
00:04:44,180 --> 00:04:46,360
Hey, Josuke, what are you doing?

69
00:04:46,760 --> 00:04:49,537
I'm just taking a quick look
through this guy's locker.

70
00:04:49,620 --> 00:04:51,032
Keep an eye out, Koichi.

71
00:04:51,420 --> 00:04:54,773
The least you could do is give
me some warning next time.

72
00:04:54,920 --> 00:04:59,380
All right, he left his bag,
so he did come back to school.

73
00:05:04,220 --> 00:05:07,220
Looks like he's in the
tennis club and a manga fan.

74
00:05:08,400 --> 00:05:11,097
And he'd be right at
home in a hoarder's club.

75
00:05:11,180 --> 00:05:15,217
I don't see how he could have hidden that
bow and arrow in here with all this shit,

76
00:05:15,300 --> 00:05:16,130
huh?

77
00:05:16,400 --> 00:05:18,165
The hell is this wooden thing?

78
00:05:21,800 --> 00:05:22,630
A sand!

79
00:05:22,860 --> 00:05:23,920
Wait, no.

80
00:05:25,300 --> 00:05:27,177
Looks like it's just an ordinary object.

81
00:05:27,260 --> 00:05:31,717
Why would this freak have one of those
wooden mannequins they sell in art stores?

82
00:05:31,800 --> 00:05:33,624
That scared the crap out of me.

83
00:05:51,500 --> 00:05:52,780
What? How?

84
00:05:53,140 --> 00:05:55,669
I touched it, and the
thing turned into me.

85
00:05:55,840 --> 00:05:58,252
Well, I guess that pretty much proves it.

86
00:06:00,240 --> 00:06:01,680
Hazemata's a stand user.

87
00:06:04,680 --> 00:06:06,260
That's just great.

88
00:06:06,580 --> 00:06:07,640
Turning into me.

89
00:06:07,860 --> 00:06:09,520
Quite the cheeky move, pal.

90
00:06:10,640 --> 00:06:12,760
The manga, Perman. You know it?

91
00:06:13,380 --> 00:06:14,500
It can speak!

92
00:06:14,720 --> 00:06:16,838
And it sounds just like you, Josuke!

93
00:06:17,300 --> 00:06:19,180
If you read Perman, you'd know.

94
00:06:19,380 --> 00:06:21,060
There's a copy robot in it.

95
00:06:21,260 --> 00:06:22,907
It's handy, don't you think?

96
00:06:23,140 --> 00:06:26,760
I bet you wish that you had
one right about now. Huh?

97
00:06:27,180 --> 00:06:29,377
Hey, Koichi, what's
this guy mumbling about?

98
00:06:29,460 --> 00:06:30,813
Who is this Perman guy?

99
00:06:31,460 --> 00:06:33,537
You're telling me you haven't read Perman?

100
00:06:33,620 --> 00:06:35,091
How's that even possible?

101
00:06:35,220 --> 00:06:36,617
Are you sure you're Japanese?

102
00:06:36,700 --> 00:06:37,530
That's enough!

103
00:06:37,613 --> 00:06:39,812
I'll be asking the questions around here!

104
00:06:40,640 --> 00:06:43,040
He's got my arm! Yusuke, no!

105
00:06:43,900 --> 00:06:46,360
However, I must give you a fair warning.

106
00:06:46,500 --> 00:06:49,500
My robot is one that you
won't want to have around.

107
00:06:51,340 --> 00:06:55,297
Once it copies you, you'll be making
all the same movements it does.

108
00:06:55,380 --> 00:06:57,980
Which means, it's really not a puppet.

109
00:06:58,220 --> 00:07:00,340
It's actually a puppet master!

110
00:07:02,920 --> 00:07:04,460
Koichi, watch out!

111
00:07:11,020 --> 00:07:11,850
Hm.

112
00:07:13,300 --> 00:07:14,130
Keicho.

113
00:07:15,260 --> 00:07:17,920
Just like that, another
one bites the dust.

114
00:07:18,160 --> 00:07:20,020
Best part, I didn't touch him.

115
00:07:20,200 --> 00:07:24,494
The honor of knocking him into Kingdom
Come goes to you, his dear friend.

116
00:07:25,300 --> 00:07:29,920
It's underhanded shit like that
that really gets my blood boiling.

117
00:07:30,660 --> 00:07:33,037
Making others do your dirty
work because you don't have

118
00:07:33,120 --> 00:07:36,355
the balls to come out and
take care of things yourself.

119
00:07:36,840 --> 00:07:39,617
Nothing makes me want to
kick someone's ass more!

120
00:07:39,700 --> 00:07:41,040
That's just great.

121
00:07:43,960 --> 00:07:47,257
It seems as though I'm outside
of your range and if you

122
00:07:47,340 --> 00:07:50,575
can't get any closer to me
then neither can your stand!

123
00:07:50,960 --> 00:07:53,777
In other words Josuke as
long as I make sure to

124
00:07:53,860 --> 00:07:56,237
always keep a little distance
between the two of us.

125
00:07:56,320 --> 00:07:59,791
You don't have a snowball's
chance in hell of defeating me!

126
00:08:03,600 --> 00:08:04,430
So,

127
00:08:04,513 --> 00:08:06,617
you know my stand's name is show-off and

128
00:08:06,700 --> 00:08:09,617
possessing this doll has
given my stand physical form.

129
00:08:09,700 --> 00:08:13,377
As a result it can now be
seen by any ordinary person!

130
00:08:13,460 --> 00:08:16,177
Damn you Hazamada!

131
00:08:16,260 --> 00:08:19,317
My objective is simple!

132
00:08:19,400 --> 00:08:22,057
Pulverize Jotaro to
within an inch of his life

133
00:08:22,140 --> 00:08:24,728
and make sure he never
returns to this town!

134
00:08:29,620 --> 00:08:35,220
He's just a pathetic outsider snooping
around and getting in our business?

135
00:08:36,760 --> 00:08:37,590
Although,

136
00:08:37,673 --> 00:08:39,117
a little birdie told me that Jotaro's Star

137
00:08:39,200 --> 00:08:41,965
Platinum can stop time
for a couple of seconds.

138
00:08:42,460 --> 00:08:46,872
There's not a single stand user among
us who can get anywhere close to him.

139
00:08:48,900 --> 00:08:53,371
Actually, the one stand that can do the
job is the one that just copied you!

140
00:08:55,080 --> 00:09:00,120
I'm taking you out of the game, but I'll
be sure to give Jotaro your regards!

141
00:09:05,320 --> 00:09:09,580
The sound of painful
squishing, it's so sublime.

142
00:09:10,040 --> 00:09:14,697
But as long as you didn't sever the nerve,
you might have a chance at seeing again.

143
00:09:14,780 --> 00:09:17,133
That is if luck decides to smile on you.

144
00:09:17,220 --> 00:09:20,037
Given his injury, I think
he'll be out for a while.

145
00:09:20,120 --> 00:09:21,460
Well, that was easy.

146
00:09:21,880 --> 00:09:23,340
Hey, pick up my bag.

147
00:09:23,740 --> 00:09:26,034
It's time to start our hunt for Jotaro.

148
00:09:27,940 --> 00:09:29,540
You made it too easy.

149
00:09:29,920 --> 00:09:33,077
Now, if I'm not mistaken,
Jotaro's hotel is...

150
00:09:33,160 --> 00:09:35,597
It's the, uh...

151
00:09:35,680 --> 00:09:37,440
The Mariah Grand Hotel!

152
00:09:37,880 --> 00:09:39,460
Oh yeah, that's it.

153
00:09:48,220 --> 00:09:49,760
Koichi! Koichi!

154
00:09:51,920 --> 00:09:53,860
Josuke, what happened?

155
00:09:54,260 --> 00:09:55,731
You're not hurt, are you?

156
00:09:55,960 --> 00:09:57,520
No, I'm doing okay.

157
00:09:57,820 --> 00:10:00,417
And you're tougher than
anyone gives you credit for.

158
00:10:00,500 --> 00:10:02,037
Even though you're all busted up,

159
00:10:02,120 --> 00:10:05,355
you still managed to tag that
imposter with your stand.

160
00:10:05,940 --> 00:10:06,940
What do you mean?

161
00:10:07,180 --> 00:10:09,651
I was only able to do that because of you.

162
00:10:09,740 --> 00:10:11,505
The moment you sent me flying,

163
00:10:11,620 --> 00:10:14,914
you healed my broken bones
with Shining Diamond's power.

164
00:10:18,740 --> 00:10:19,570
But,

165
00:10:19,653 --> 00:10:23,617
uh, do you think you could heal the
injuries I got when I slammed into the door?

166
00:10:23,700 --> 00:10:26,876
I don't want to be a bother,
but I'm in a lot of pain.

167
00:10:27,660 --> 00:10:28,490
You bet.

168
00:10:53,920 --> 00:10:57,577
you've reached the Mariah
grand hotel yeah hi how's it

169
00:10:57,660 --> 00:11:01,680
going i need jotaro kujo He
should be staying in room 324.

170
00:11:02,100 --> 00:11:03,218
One moment, please.

171
00:11:05,260 --> 00:11:06,200
Hurry up!

172
00:11:06,400 --> 00:11:07,457
We have to tell Mr.

173
00:11:07,540 --> 00:11:09,997
Jotaro about that stand
before it's too late!

174
00:11:10,080 --> 00:11:11,374
Thank you for waiting.

175
00:11:11,720 --> 00:11:14,460
Unfortunately, the line
for room 324 is busy.

176
00:11:15,280 --> 00:11:17,240
You can try calling again later.

177
00:11:17,940 --> 00:11:18,880
It's busy?

178
00:11:19,400 --> 00:11:20,560
What?! Of course!

179
00:11:20,820 --> 00:11:22,437
He must be talking to the copy!

180
00:11:22,520 --> 00:11:23,720
This is just great!

181
00:11:23,900 --> 00:11:25,076
It got to him first!

182
00:11:26,640 --> 00:11:27,900
You sure, Josuke?

183
00:11:28,760 --> 00:11:31,617
Hey, you found proof that there's
another stand user at your school?

184
00:11:31,700 --> 00:11:32,530
That I have.

185
00:11:32,800 --> 00:11:34,800
I'll fill you in at Mariah Station.

186
00:11:35,360 --> 00:11:37,277
Let's meet at the square in front.

187
00:11:37,360 --> 00:11:39,242
You can get there in 15 minutes.

188
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:40,830
Understood.

189
00:11:40,913 --> 00:11:43,115
See you in front of the station in 15.

190
00:11:45,980 --> 00:11:47,140
Easy as pie.

191
00:11:55,000 --> 00:11:57,337
Shit! No answer. This is bad.

192
00:11:57,420 --> 00:11:58,617
He must have left, then.

193
00:11:58,700 --> 00:12:02,077
Which means they probably baited
Jotaro to go and meet them somewhere.

194
00:12:02,160 --> 00:12:02,990
Damn.

195
00:12:03,073 --> 00:12:05,137
All we can do now is go after the copy.

196
00:12:05,220 --> 00:12:06,050
What do we do?

197
00:12:06,220 --> 00:12:08,697
I couldn't tell you two
apart to save my life.

198
00:12:08,780 --> 00:12:09,610
Yeah.

199
00:12:09,693 --> 00:12:11,437
Stealing my face is weird enough.

200
00:12:11,520 --> 00:12:14,177
But what really freaks
me out are his fingers.

201
00:12:14,260 --> 00:12:18,217
How often do you catch a glimpse of
your fingers compared to your face?

202
00:12:18,300 --> 00:12:21,771
I realize that standard copied
me down to the finger press.

203
00:12:23,380 --> 00:12:24,210
Huh?

204
00:12:24,293 --> 00:12:25,123
Hey, Josuke.

205
00:12:25,280 --> 00:12:26,339
You're back early.

206
00:12:26,760 --> 00:12:28,054
Where's Master Koichi?

207
00:12:29,320 --> 00:12:31,849
Hazamada, what the heck
are you doing here?

208
00:12:32,000 --> 00:12:33,800
Tamami Kobayashi, huh?

209
00:12:35,200 --> 00:12:37,560
You have no idea why we're hanging out?

210
00:12:37,780 --> 00:12:39,320
Come on, give it a guess.

211
00:12:39,840 --> 00:12:41,120
I'm all guessed out!

212
00:12:41,840 --> 00:12:44,400
So you don't even have one little theory?

213
00:12:45,320 --> 00:12:46,740
Should I have one, sir?

214
00:12:47,600 --> 00:12:48,600
Nah, you're good.

215
00:12:53,940 --> 00:12:54,980
Step on it.

216
00:13:00,060 --> 00:13:03,940
If we don't hurry and catch up
with Hazamada, Jotaro is done for!

217
00:13:15,340 --> 00:13:19,177
We can't let Jotaro meet up with the
copier, it'll be a total disaster!

218
00:13:19,260 --> 00:13:24,025
Yeah, but I haven't figured out a solution
yet, so for now, all we can do is run!

219
00:13:31,380 --> 00:13:33,145
We'll catch you later, Josuke.

220
00:13:33,400 --> 00:13:35,580
See you tomorrow. Yeah, take it easy.

221
00:13:36,940 --> 00:13:38,200
See you yet, Josuke.

222
00:13:38,320 --> 00:13:39,160
Bye, Josuke.

223
00:13:39,320 --> 00:13:40,496
Have a good evening.

224
00:13:40,960 --> 00:13:44,417
Why the hell are these chattering
schoolgirls only saying goodbye to you?

225
00:13:44,500 --> 00:13:48,676
No one ever says stuff like that to
me when I leave school for the day.

226
00:13:49,300 --> 00:13:53,006
Why should I care since every
girl in this school is butt-ugly?

227
00:13:53,880 --> 00:13:54,937
Josuke? Huh?

228
00:13:55,020 --> 00:13:56,940
Um, could you read this?

229
00:13:59,280 --> 00:14:00,760
Well, bye then!

230
00:14:02,060 --> 00:14:06,060
Why are you accepting notes from
her, like it would do you any good?

231
00:14:07,260 --> 00:14:08,090
Goddammit!

232
00:14:08,173 --> 00:14:11,017
What the hell makes a jerk
like you so special anyway?

233
00:14:11,100 --> 00:14:12,100
What's your deal?

234
00:14:12,360 --> 00:14:14,889
The show's over now,
so let's just move on.

235
00:14:15,200 --> 00:14:18,417
Maybe you've forgotten, but we
don't have time to dilly-dally.

236
00:14:18,500 --> 00:14:20,500
How dare you speak to me that way!

237
00:14:21,020 --> 00:14:21,937
That hurts!

238
00:14:22,020 --> 00:14:25,020
Punching a guy made of wood
was bound to end badly.

239
00:14:25,140 --> 00:14:26,905
That was pretty stupid of you.

240
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:29,176
Shut the hell up and cry crowding me!

241
00:14:29,620 --> 00:14:30,450
Damn it.

242
00:14:30,540 --> 00:14:32,277
He's really starting to get to me.

243
00:14:32,360 --> 00:14:34,360
This always happens with my stand.

244
00:14:34,540 --> 00:14:37,364
Like when I copied my
crush Junko the other day.

245
00:14:37,640 --> 00:14:39,640
She morphed into a complete bitch.

246
00:14:39,900 --> 00:14:42,900
I couldn't take it, so the
entire thing was a flop.

247
00:14:43,080 --> 00:14:46,374
Is there no one halfway decent
on this miserable planet?

248
00:14:46,920 --> 00:14:48,920
That damn Josuke'll get his.

249
00:14:49,100 --> 00:14:51,017
But first I have to take care of Jotaro.

250
00:14:51,100 --> 00:14:53,000
I'll crush him into paste.

251
00:14:54,360 --> 00:14:55,780
This is gonna be good!

252
00:14:57,240 --> 00:14:58,070
Huh?

253
00:14:58,200 --> 00:15:01,397
You've got to be kidding that
guy smudged my motorcycle

254
